  "narrative": "This is the First Friday feeder special of the Fall. No recent Friday feeder specials to make any market comparison. Feeder calves all sold on good demand for light to moderate offerings. Yearlings sold on mostly good to very good demand for light to moderate offerings. Cooperate packer buyers showed good demand for green, high quality yearlings today as several long strings of attractive cattle off grass were seen. Additionally several backgrounded offerings out of grow lots were seen and demand for these offerings was moderate to good. Most grow lot offerings were in moderate to moderate plus; a few discounted offerings were seen and marked as fleshy. Feeder calves are starting to be marketed and demand for calves was mostly good. Lots of variation of quality was noticed today. Most calves were in small to moderate size packages, forcing buyers to piece together loads. Demand was good from private feeders and Canadian buyers. Cooperate packers were mostly sidelined today as they showed limited interest in new crop calves. A large crowd of buyers was on hand for todays sale with over 15 different buyers actively bidding on offerings. Market activity was mostly active as a result. Weigh up cows sold on light demand for very light offerings. Too few cows and bulls were seen to develop any market trend. Supply included: 99% Feeder Cattle (42% Steers, 56% Heifers, 2% Bulls); 0% Slaughter Cattle (88% Cows, 13% Bulls); 0% Replacement Cattle (100% Stock Cows). Feeder cattle supply over 600 lbs was 51%.",
